<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Crisis</p><h1 class="enc-title">Panic of 1890</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1890</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Baring crisis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Panic of 1890, also called the Baring crisis, was a financial crisis set off when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> bank <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barings-bank">Baring Brothers</a>, heavily exposed to Argentine bonds, came close to collapse. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bank-of-england">Bank of England</a> organised a rescue that prevented a wider panic in London. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a> it brought a deep depression and the fall of President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miguel-juarez-celman">Miguel Juárez Celman</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/panic-of-1890.jpg" alt="Panic of 1890" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ernesto de la Cárcova · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ernesto_de_la_C%C3%A1rcova_-_Sin_pan_y_sin_trabajo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
